## Headline

Median over 28 cells with a genuine config difference: penalty 1.029, 90% bootstrap interval over cells [1.003, 1.053].

In words: fallback is 2.9% SLOWER than tuned. A deployment on a (model, shard, card) with no tuned vLLM config runs the fallback ladder and pays 2.9% more time per MoE layer than the same layer on the same card with a tuned file.

Verdict band: FOOTNOTE (FOOTNOTE <1.05, MODEST <1.15, MATERIAL >=1.15).

## Gates

[PASS] G0 same-layer  every arm computes the same MoE layer as the native one
         gate: max relative error vs native <= 0.02
         saw:  max rel err 0.00e+00
[PASS] G1 derivation  vLLM v0.27.1 loads the config tile_resolve DERIVES
         gate: zero cells where the observed native config differs from the derived one
         saw:  0 mismatches over 28 observed cells
[PASS] G2 override  override_config actually forces the config it is given
         gate: zero arms where the recorder saw a config other than the forced one
         saw:  0 of 127 forced arms ran a config they were not given
[FAIL] G3 placebo  re-timing the SAME config moves the answer by almost nothing
         gate: p90 of |replica/native - 1| < 3%
         saw:  p90 placebo deviation 3.62% over 28 cells
[PASS] G4 sign  the tuned config is not SLOWER than its own fallback
         gate: median penalty >= 1.00
         saw:  median penalty 1.029 -- fallback is 2.9% SLOWER than tuned
[FAIL] G5 size  the fallback costs at least 15%
